During further investigation, two attachments were identified within the email.

Attachment 1 — text/plain
The first attachment was identified as text/plain and contained Base64-encoded data.
The Base64 content was decoded using CyberChef to uncover and examine the underlying content.

Attachment 2 — application/pdf
The second attachment was identified as application/pdf. Further analysis of the attachment revealed that its underlying file format was not a conventional PDF.
The Base64-encoded content was processed using CyberChef and converted to hexadecimal for file signature analysis.
The hexadecimal file signature was compared against the Gary Kessler File Signature Table, which indicated that the underlying file was a ZIP archive.

ZIP Archive Analysis
The identified ZIP archive was extracted for further investigation.

The archive contained the following files:
•	Excel file
•	JPEG image
•	PDF file
